{"id": "0007917_p0046", "tianyige_id": "0007917", "title": "萬曆十年江北武舉鄉試錄", "western_year": 1582, "reign_era": "萬曆", "reign_year": 10, "exam_level": "provincial (鄉試)", "military": true, "province": "江北", "province_en": "Jiangbei", "page": 46, "scan_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=File%3ATianyige-330000-1705-0007917_%E8%90%AC%E6%9B%86%E5%8D%81%E5%B9%B4%E6%B1%9F%E5%8C%97%E6%AD%A6%E8%88%89%E9%84%89%E8%A9%A6%E9%8C%84_%E6%98%8E%E8%90%AC%E6%9B%86%E5%88%BB%E6%9C%AC.pdf&page=46", "text": "衝難矣又一日而用之帷幄\n之中觀變察萌使兵不血刃\n而坐收全勝之利則運籌者\n又難之難矣今多士既以其\n馳射方畧稱千人之雄登名\n司馬則所難入彀者免也第\n自今以往其致用益鉅則竭\n===\n才而副之益難諸士試度而\n智勇劵之異日謂能任不耶\n夫智不必至誠極則通勇不\n必兼忠激則奮以周之僕夫\n從征朔方見大將有悄悄心\n亦爲之况瘁不遑啟處執干\n戈以衛社稷丈夫事也乃魯", "banxin": ["武舉録後序　四"], "ocr_model": "claude-opus-5-5 (agy, low effort)", "blank": false, "has_examiner_comments": false, "chatter_stripped": false, "alt_text": null, "alt_ocr_model": null, "agreement": null, "punctuated": "衝，難矣；又一日而用之帷幄之中，觀變察萌，使兵不血刃而坐收全勝之利，則運籌者又難之難矣。今多士既以其馳射、方畧稱千人之雄，登名司馬，則所難入彀者免也。第自今以往，其致用益鉅，則竭才而副之益難。諸士試度而智勇劵之異日，謂能任不耶？夫智不必至，誠極則通；勇不必兼，忠激則奮。以周之僕夫從征朔方，見大將有悄悄心，亦爲之况瘁，不遑啟處。執干戈以衛社稷，丈夫事也，乃魯", "translation_en": "…charge in the vanguard, it is already difficult; and if one day they are employed within the commander's tent to observe shifting circumstances and discern incipient signs, causing the soldiers' blades to remain unbloodied while sitting back to reap the benefits of complete victory, then for those who devise strategies, it is the most difficult of difficulties. Now that the many gentlemen have already been acclaimed as heroes among a thousand men by virtue of their mounted archery and strategic planning, and have had their names entered on the rolls of the Minister of War, they are spared the difficulty of failing to enter the bowshot range of selection. Yet from this day forward, as the responsibilities to which they are put become ever greater, exhausting their talents to live up to them becomes ever more difficult. Let all you gentlemen try to take the measure of your wisdom and courage and pledge them against a future day: would you say you are capable of bearing the task or not? Now, wisdom need not be consummate—when sincerity reaches its utmost, comprehension follows; courage need not surpass all others—when loyalty is aroused, ardor is stirred. Take the grooms of the Zhou dynasty who followed the expedition to the northern regions: seeing that their great general harbored an anxious heart, they too grew worn and haggard on his account, having no leisure to rest in peace. Taking up shield and spear to defend the altars of soil and grain is the proper business of a stalwart man, yet in Lu…", "translation_model": "gemini-4-argon-low (agy)"}
